===== conclusion =====
TEXT (Text2CAD test, n=200): IoU 82.5% / median CD 0.19 / IR 3.0% vs paper Tab. 1 82.1 / 0.20 / 1.4 -> reproduces the paper within IoU +-5 pp, IR <= +3 pp, CD +-0.1 (our convention: validity 97.0%, bbox-Chamfer 0.038, F 0.868, op-type recall 0.99; on ComplexCAD the same branch gave 89.2% / 0.422 / 0.044 / 0.23). The text adapter is intact; the ComplexCAD text result is a domain gap. IMAGES (DeepCAD test): with the venv's qwen-vl-utils 0.0.14 (n=200) IoU 39.1% / CD 4.91 / IR 4.0% (validity 95.5%, bbox-Chamfer 0.085, F 0.402); with the Dockerfile-pinned qwen-vl-utils 0.0.10 (n=100) IoU 86.2% / CD 0.17 / IR 1.0% (validity 99.0%, bbox-Chamfer 0.021, F 0.943) vs paper 86.1 / 0.18 / 1.5 -> reproduces the paper under the same tolerance. The image adapter is intact once the pinned qwen-vl-utils is used; our ComplexCAD image-mode rows were run with the mismatched 144-token grid and mix a tokenisation mismatch with the render-style domain gap, so they should be re-run with 0.0.10 before being interpreted.
